1. Bit: Interacts with Transmission (to transmit torque), Motor (to receive rotational force), and External Environment (as it comes into contact with the material being drilled).
2. Transmission: Interacts with Bit (to transmit torque) and Motor (to receive rotational force).
3. Motor: Interacts with Transmission (to provide rotational force), Electrical System (to receive power), and Battery Holder (as it is powered by the battery).
4. Electrical System: Interacts with Motor (to supply power) and Battery Holder (as it manages the electrical connection to the battery).
5. Battery Holder: Interacts with Motor (as it powers the motor), Electrical System (for managing the electrical connection), and Housing (since it is part of the housing assembly).
6. Housing: Interacts with Battery Holder (since it houses the battery holder) and External Environment (as it protects internal components from external factors).
7. External Environment: Interacts with Bit (as mentioned above), Housing (as mentioned above), and all other components indirectly as they are affected by environmental conditions such as temperature, humidity, etc.

Based on this analysis, the DSM can be represented as follows:
```python
