- The Transmission interacts with the Bit, Motor, and Electrical System. It is housed within the Housing but does not directly interact with the Battery Holder or External Environment.
- The Motor interacts with the Bit, Transmission, and Electrical System. Like the Transmission, it is housed within the Housing but does not directly interact with the Battery Holder or External Environment.
- The Electrical System interacts with the Bit, Transmission, Motor, Battery Holder (for power), and Housing (for support). It does not directly interact with the External Environment.
- The Battery Holder only interacts with the Electrical System and is housed within the Housing. It does not directly interact with the Bit, Transmission, Motor, or External Environment.
- The Housing interacts with all components as it houses them but does not directly interact with the External Environment.
- The External Environment only interacts with the Bit and Housing (for support).
